Derived work: hashicorp/go-memdb
===========================================================================

go-maemmidb is a derivative work of go-memdb:

    https://github.com/hashicorp/go-memdb
    Copyright (c) 2015 HashiCorp, Inc.
    Copyright IBM Corp. 2015, 2026
    Licensed under the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0

Baseline: upstream commit 7d3fdd5 (v1.3.5 plus header/CI-only commits).

The public API, its documentation, its observable behaviour, and the test
suite of this project originate from go-memdb. Files fall into three groups:

  Verbatim copies (byte-identical to upstream, checksums in
  scripts/upstream-verbatim.sha256):
    schema.go filter.go changes.go
    filter_test.go index_test.go integ_test.go isolation_test.go
    memdb_test.go schema_test.go txn_test.go watch_test.go

  Derived and modified (upstream copyright and SPDX header retained, a
  "Modifications Copyright" line and provenance comment added):
    memdb.go index.go txn.go watch.go watch_few.go watch-gen/main.go

  New work (Copyright (c) 2026 Ville Vesilehto, MPL-2.0):
    everything else, including benchmarks/. The storage engine is the
    separate module github.com/thevilledev/go-juuri (same author, same
    licence).

===========================================================================
Studied work: hashicorp/go-immutable-radix
===========================================================================

    https://github.com/hashicorp/go-immutable-radix
    Copyright (c) 2015 HashiCorp, Inc.
    Licensed under the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0

go-memdb stores its indexes in go-immutable-radix (v1.3.1). This project
replaces it with a new radix tree, go-juuri, written from scratch. The
observable semantics of go-immutable-radix -- iteration order, prefix and
lower-bound seeks, longest-prefix matching and the granularity at which watch
channels fire -- were studied and are deliberately reproduced so that
go-maemmidb stays behaviourally compatible with go-memdb. No source code of
go-immutable-radix is included in the main module or in go-juuri.

